<!--
    structheadless: a record read only past its start is synthesized only in a
    function whose callers are all known direct calls.

    The CLI fixture decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/structheadless_x86_64
    has a reader of three members of a record, none of them the first:

        struct entry { char *name; long size; unsigned int mode;
                       unsigned int link; char ok; char linkok; };
        unsigned int mode_of(const struct entry *e)
        { return (e->linkok && e->size > 0) ? e->link : e->mode; }

        80 7f 19 00       cmp    byte [rdi+0x19],0
        74 12             je     +0x12
        48 83 7f 08 00    cmp    qword [rdi+0x8],0
        7e 0b             jle    +0xb
        8b 47 14          mov    eax,[rdi+0x14]
        c3                ret
        0f 1f 80 00 00 00 00
        8b 47 10          mov    eax,[rdi+0x10]
        c3                ret

    NEGATIVE CONTROL. `closed` gives such a parameter a record only where a
    whole-binary `decompile-all` recorded every caller of the function as a
    direct call. This harness decompiles ONE function from a byte image, so
    nothing marks it closed and it must read the same in both passes: reads
    through an untyped pointer and no synthesized record. A rule that took
    a headless record here would do the same to a qsort comparator, whose
    contract declares `void *`.

    The two-pass coverage over the whole binary-to-decompile path is
    tests/cli/structheadless-off-leaves-a-headless-record-untyped.json (off)
    and structheadless-closed-reads-a-record-past-its-start.json (closed).

    Stage / sub-stage: P5 "aggregate-union". Pass 1 pins `off`, pass 2 `closed`.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
807f1900741248837f08007e0b8b4714c30f1f80000000008b4710c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="mode_of"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>option structheadless off</com>
  <com>lo fu mode_of</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option structheadless closed</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
